# Phase deploy workflow (automated)

When you **finish a development phase** and the user has not said "don't deploy", run this workflow **before ending the turn**.

Static site — **no local npm build** (Vercel runs `build.sh`). Script skips build preflight.

## 1. Ask which environment

| Option | When to use |
|--------|-------------|
| **Preview** (`development`) | HTML changes before production |
| **Production** (`master`) | Ready for nasneeraj.com |
| **Skip deploy** | Local-only edits |

Default: **Preview** unless user asked for production.

## 2. Commit if needed

- Commit only when user asked or phase includes shipping.
- Never commit LFS pointers without actual assets.

## 3. Run phase deploy

```powershell
npm run phase:deploy -- --env preview
npm run phase:deploy -- --env production
```

On failure: read Vercel logs → fix → commit → re-run.

## 4. Branch reference

| Env | Branch | URL |
|-----|--------|-----|
| Preview | `development` | Vercel preview |
| Production | `master` | https://nasneeraj.com |

**Note:** Remote also has `main`; active production branch is **`master`**.

Config: `scripts/phase-deploy.config.json`
